    <string name="help_title">How to use RadarTren</string>
    <string name="help_dots_title">Each dot is a train</string>
    <string name="help_dots_body">The colour tells you if it is on time. Tap a dot to see where it is going and how late it is.</string>
    <string name="help_rings_title">A circle around it is a problem</string>
    <string name="help_rings_body">It can be a very late train or many late trains in one area. At the top you see how many problems there are now. Tap it to see the list.</string>
    <string name="help_search_title">Find your station</string>
    <string name="help_search_body">Tap the magnifying glass and type your station or your line, for example C4 or Atocha.</string>
    <string name="help_alerts_title">Alerts on your phone</string>
    <string name="help_alerts_body">If there is a serious problem, your phone tells you even with the app closed. You can change this in Settings.</string>
    <string name="help_trouble_title">If your train is having problems</string>
    <string name="help_trouble_body">Ask the station staff or call Renfe. RadarTren only informs: it cannot change anything about the trains.</string>
    <string name="help_call_renfe">Call Renfe (912 320 320)</string>
    <string name="help_call_112">Emergencies: call 112</string>
